Subject: [PATCH 2/2] AgiBot Full ABD, CUDA 12.8 and wheel build support

Base: 292c98c3fec2dfbe9ae2c2407572f2f446a4a738 (official libuipc v0.0.25).
Apply 0001-nvidia-optimizations.patch first, then this patch, with git apply.
Copyright (c) 2023-2026, AgiBot Inc. All Rights Reserved.
Author: Genie Sim Team
License: Mozilla Public License Version 2.0

Identified AgiBot contributions retain MPL-2.0; NVIDIA Full ABD follow-up,
libuipc, Eigen and third-party contributions keep their original notices.
Component notices and original license texts are retained in the patches
and the official baseline.

CUDA 12.8 variant: SM89 and SM120; wheel version uses cu128. CUDA 13
builds must not be repackaged as cu128. Build in a fresh directory using
CUDA 12.8 headers/libraries and matching native outputs. The source-level
thrust::counting_iterator compatibility change remains valid in CUDA 12.8.
This variant has static/recipe checks only; no native build or GPU validation.

Build entry: tools/wheel_cuda128/build_wheels.py (add --dry-run for a plan).
Use CPython 3.12, GCC/G++ 11, CMake 3.26+, Ninja and CUDA 12.8.
First build clean dependencies with tools/wheel_cuda128/build_dependencies.py.
Example after supplying the external dependency paths:
  python3.12 tools/wheel_cuda128/build_wheels.py --arch both \
    --cuda-root /usr/local/cuda-12.8 --work-dir /build/uipc-cu128 \
    --dependency-prefix /opt/deps/x64-linux --vcpkg-root /opt/vcpkg \
    --clean-dependency-lib /build/third-party/install/lib
Package with tools/wheel_cuda128/package_wheel.py using the same --cuda-root
and native build directory sm89-cu128/build or sm120-cu128/build.

